<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103524" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετράρχ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tetrarch</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				12.5.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				416
			</span></i> (Cos, i. <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				543.3
			</span></i> (Ancyra, <span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>), etc.; of rulers under the
			protection of Rome of lower grade than kings, e.g. in Palestine,
				<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				14.1
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				1.12.5
			</span></i>, al.; generally, Sall.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.</u>
				20.7
			</span></i>, Hor.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Sat.</u>
				1.3.12
			</span></i>, etc.: also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέτραρχος</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θεσσαλῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					274
				</span></i>
			 (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>): gen. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-χου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					606.4
				</span></i>
			 (Syria, <span class="entity">i A.D.</span>), but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-χα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IGRom.</u>
					4.1683
				</span></i>
			 (Pergam.): cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετραρχία</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a leader of four</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόχοι</span>, or <i><span class="en">
				64
			</span></i> men, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rev.Arch.</u>
				3
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				1934
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				40
			</span></i> (Amphipolis, <span class="entity">iii/ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				6(1935).31
			</span></i> (ibid., <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				2.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				10.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>Tact.</u>
				9.2
			</span></i>.</div>
